WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.868
Welcome to this week's "Imseriou"

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:03.503
This week's episode features

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:06.406
a long-distance filming trip across different counties and cities

00:00:06.406 --> 00:00:07.640
in northern, central, and southern Taiwan

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.042
. Today's topic is about solar panels

00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:10.643
from an industrial engineering perspective.

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:12.912
Every time solar panels are mentioned

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:14.814
, it sparks a lot of political debate.

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:16.950
People start talking about "green electricity," "cockroaches," "

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:18.985
solar panels flying around during typhoons,"

00:00:18.985 --> 00:00:20.587
"fishery-electricity symbiosis in central and southern

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:22.489
Taiwan," and "fake aquaculture, real money-making schemes,"

00:00:22.489 --> 00:00:24.791
among various other names. There are also

00:00:24.791 --> 00:00:27.127
many misconceptions about solar panels

00:00:27.127 --> 00:00:28.695
online. Since we

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:29.696
've filmed solar panels

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:31.264
in previous episodes

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:33.333
, the online discussions have been very heated

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:34.501
and intense.

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:35.702
So, in this episode, we'll focus on

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:38.538
many frequently discussed topics

00:00:38.538 --> 00:00:39.873
and conduct on-site measurements

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:41.474
to show you the real situation.

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:42.208
Because in our...

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:43.676
From an industrial engineering perspective,

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:44.844
many things

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:46.246
are actually done incorrectly.

00:00:46.246 --> 00:00:47.781
Does Taiwan have "green energy cockroaches" (corruption thieves)?

00:00:47.781 --> 00:00:48.948
Definitely, there are

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:49.849
quite a few.

00:00:49.849 --> 00:00:50.550
But

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.485
is the problem with the solar panels themselves?

00:00:52.485 --> 00:00:54.354
I have a different view.

00:00:54.354 --> 00:00:56.122
For example, besides "green energy cockroaches,"

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:58.491
Taiwan also has many construction and

00:00:58.491 --> 00:00:59.759
decoration cockroaches

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:02.295
who exploit certain things for profit

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:03.229
, engaging in reckless

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:05.398
practices to gain substantial benefits.

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:06.933
Is there a problem with the solar panels themselves?

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:07.934
I think we can

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:09.169
look at it from another angle

00:01:09.169 --> 00:01:10.103
. For instance, I personally believe

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:11.771
there's nothing wrong with solar panels themselves.

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:12.672
You're not using them

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:14.007
to haphazardly create problems

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:16.176
or to claim government subsidies

00:01:16.176 --> 00:01:18.478
; you're genuinely utilizing the

00:01:18.478 --> 00:01:20.980
energy resources that are sprinkled on the earth every day.

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:21.614
Look at

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:23.116
the weather outside now...

00:01:23.116 --> 00:01:24.517
The sun is so hot that it's easily

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:25.985
30-40 degrees Celsius

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:28.421
outside. If you could collect all that

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:30.623
energy lost every day and

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:31.991
convert it into electricity

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:32.725
or

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:34.294
money ,

00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:35.462
I think there's nothing wrong with that.

00:01:35.462 --> 00:01:36.262
However, online,

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:37.864
you've probably heard

00:01:37.864 --> 00:01:39.365
a lot about the problems and environmental impacts

00:01:39.365 --> 00:01:40.900
of solar panels.

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:43.603
Today, we'll take you to different counties and cities, to

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:44.704
different sites

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:47.574
, even to the south, to see

00:01:47.574 --> 00:01:48.641
aquaculture-electro-solar coexistence

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:50.276
. We'll use on-site measurements

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:52.345
and explain it

00:01:52.345 --> 00:01:53.279
from an industrial engineering perspective.

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:54.747
Then you can evaluate

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:57.016
whether this is different from what you

00:01:57.016 --> 00:01:58.852
've seen and heard online

00:01:58.852 --> 00:02:00.086
. Our first stop

00:02:00.086 --> 00:02:02.689
is on a netizen's rooftop.

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:04.057
Now we've arrived at our first...

00:02:04.057 --> 00:02:06.392
The first misconception many people have online is about

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:07.961
solar panels on their

00:02:07.961 --> 00:02:08.895
ceilings,

00:02:08.895 --> 00:02:10.063
roofs, and rooftops

00:02:10.063 --> 00:02:11.264
. Whenever we mention this,

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:12.432
several problems arise.

00:02:12.432 --> 00:02:13.199
The first is

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:15.034
the typhoon season, when everything flies around

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:17.003
, or solar panels get sprayed onto people

00:02:17.003 --> 00:02:17.971
and hit them.

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:18.671
Firstly, this is

00:02:18.671 --> 00:02:19.472
an installation issue.

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:20.507
We've discussed

00:02:20.507 --> 00:02:21.574
this in previous episodes of

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:22.642
our solar energy series.

00:02:22.642 --> 00:02:23.910
As long as the solar panels

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:25.512
aren't haphazardly fastened to asbestos roofing, but instead secured

00:02:25.512 --> 00:02:27.080
with

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:29.949
self-tapping screws to the sheet metal of a tin roof, and

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:31.417
as long as the structure is properly built

00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:32.719
and fixed

00:02:32.719 --> 00:02:33.887
in a steel frame

00:02:33.887 --> 00:02:34.621
, there's generally

00:02:34.621 --> 00:02:35.855
not much to fear,

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:37.657
unless there's

00:02:37.657 --> 00:02:39.058
a typhoon stronger than usual.

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:40.493
The second misconception

00:02:40.493 --> 00:02:41.628
is about the urban heat island effect.

00:02:41.628 --> 00:02:42.795
First, let's explain the

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:43.963
true urban heat island effect.

00:02:43.963 --> 00:02:45.598
It refers to the fact that urban temperatures

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:48.268
are often more than 5 degrees Celsius higher than suburban temperatures.

00:02:48.268 --> 00:02:50.637
This is mainly due to the higher building density in cities,

00:02:50.637 --> 00:02:52.005
such as asphalt roads absorbing heat

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:52.906
, and the lack of vegetation

00:02:52.906 --> 00:02:54.541
, leading to heat

00:02:54.541 --> 00:02:55.675
accumulation and difficulty in dissipating.

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:56.409
This effect

00:02:56.409 --> 00:02:58.478
can affect localized rainfall.

00:02:58.478 --> 00:03:01.514
Rainfall is primarily related to the amount of moisture in the air and

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:03.449
the location of fronts .

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:06.252
According to scholars from Taiwan's FactCheck Center,

00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:07.387
fronts have a spatial scale of

00:03:07.387 --> 00:03:09.189
hundreds to thousands of kilometers

00:03:09.189 --> 00:03:11.024
, and the main frontal factors affecting Taiwan

00:03:11.024 --> 00:03:12.025
are the Pacific High, the

00:03:12.025 --> 00:03:14.594
convection system originating from the Qinghai-Tibet Plateau, and

00:03:14.594 --> 00:03:15.562
the southwest monsoon

00:03:15.562 --> 00:03:17.063
. Therefore, the principle of solar panels

00:03:17.063 --> 00:03:18.464
is to convert solar energy

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:19.966
into... The solar panels

00:03:19.966 --> 00:03:21.401
have virtually no relation

00:03:21.401 --> 00:03:22.635
to the so-called heat island effect.

00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:23.203
They basically

00:03:23.203 --> 00:03:24.637
don't raise the overall ambient temperature

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:26.005
, nor do they affect heat convection.

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:27.106
However,

00:03:27.106 --> 00:03:28.374
the reason we chose this location for filming

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:29.475
is because it's a very special site

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:31.144
. Our producer

00:03:31.144 --> 00:03:31.878
found it through Threads.

00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:32.979
Usually, when we need to explain

00:03:32.979 --> 00:03:34.480
online rumors,

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:36.082
we need experimental data

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:37.517
, a formal filming location

00:03:37.517 --> 00:03:38.718
, and some experimental scenes.

00:03:38.718 --> 00:03:40.053
So, we found

00:03:40.053 --> 00:03:42.155
a building with the same architecture and building materials

00:03:42.155 --> 00:03:43.356
—a continuous building.

00:03:43.356 --> 00:03:44.958
See, the shaded area here

00:03:44.958 --> 00:03:45.959
actually has solar panels.

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:47.427
The left side has

00:03:47.427 --> 00:03:49.762
them, the right side doesn't.

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:51.831
We also need to measure the temperature on both sides—

00:03:51.831 --> 00:03:53.566
the shaded side and the unshaded

00:03:53.566 --> 00:03:54.867
side—presumably. The difference will be significant

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:56.336
, but I'm measuring a different kind of temperature—

00:03:56.336 --> 00:03:58.504
the indoor temperature inside

00:03:58.504 --> 00:03:59.739
the ceiling of this building.

00:03:59.739 --> 00:04:01.074
The difference will be substantial.

00:04:01.074 --> 00:04:02.041
Why did I film this

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:03.543
? Because in previous videos,

00:04:03.543 --> 00:04:05.311
some people mentioned that installing solar panels

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:06.813
turned their homes into ovens,

00:04:06.813 --> 00:04:09.048
while not installing them resulted in better ventilation and cooler temperatures.

00:04:09.048 --> 00:04:09.849
This is incorrect.

00:04:09.849 --> 00:04:10.416
Why?

00:04:10.416 --> 00:04:11.651
First, we need to go back to

00:04:11.651 --> 00:04:13.653
the installation method in this project

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:14.754
. If the solar panels aren't

00:04:14.754 --> 00:04:16.589
completely flush against the building

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:18.224
or directly mounted on a metal shed, and

00:04:18.224 --> 00:04:19.192
you haven't created a

00:04:19.192 --> 00:04:20.493
space for heat convection,

00:04:20.493 --> 00:04:22.395
then heat may indeed accumulate.

00:04:22.395 --> 00:04:23.630
However, if the installation method is correct

00:04:23.630 --> 00:04:25.131
and you create a heat convection layer,

00:04:25.131 --> 00:04:27.100
you'll find that

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:29.269
when the heat convection doesn't accumulate there,

00:04:29.269 --> 00:04:30.003
it will be cooler

00:04:30.003 --> 00:04:31.237
. And it has a shading effect

00:04:31.237 --> 00:04:32.505
. Besides making your house

00:04:32.505 --> 00:04:33.740
less prone to leaks,

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:34.974
this shading effect

00:04:34.974 --> 00:04:37.110
also helps cool your building.

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:38.311
First, let me

00:04:38.311 --> 00:04:40.813
explain why it helps your house stay healthier

00:04:40.813 --> 00:04:42.382
and last longer.

00:04:42.382 --> 00:04:43.116
One reason is that

00:04:43.116 --> 00:04:45.218
if you build a gazebo on your roof,

00:04:45.218 --> 00:04:47.287
it achieves the same effect

00:04:47.287 --> 00:04:49.188
. Because of ultraviolet radiation, sun exposure

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:51.424
won't cause your waterproofing layer to age faster.

00:04:51.424 --> 00:04:53.493
Roofs usually have a waterproofing layer,

00:04:53.493 --> 00:04:55.628
which is a way to reduce UV damage.

00:04:55.628 --> 00:04:56.929
Another reason is that

00:04:56.929 --> 00:04:58.831
when there's a thermal convection layer

00:04:58.831 --> 00:05:00.099
, the heat energy

00:05:00.099 --> 00:05:02.735
won't directly hit your building.

00:05:02.735 --> 00:05:04.337
So if we measure the temperature here,

00:05:05.204 --> 00:05:06.706
is it hot today?

00:05:06.706 --> 00:05:08.641
Even standing under it...

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:10.410
Both are 36.7 degrees Celsius. That means

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:12.712
the roof temperature

00:05:12.712 --> 00:05:13.946
of the household with solar panels

00:05:13.946 --> 00:05:16.449
is 36.7 degrees Celsius.

00:05:16.449 --> 00:05:18.685
Okay, let's move

00:05:18.685 --> 00:05:20.453
on to the neighboring household without cutting

00:05:20.853 --> 00:05:23.156
anything . The neighboring household

00:05:23.156 --> 00:05:24.557
has less shade.

00:05:26.559 --> 00:05:27.694
Why is it so hot today ?

00:05:27.694 --> 00:05:28.361
People are out working,

00:05:28.361 --> 00:05:29.762
aren't they afraid of the sun?

00:05:29.762 --> 00:05:30.663
What's the temperature now

00:05:30.663 --> 00:05:31.798
? It 's only 37.3 degrees

00:05:31.798 --> 00:05:33.132
Celsius, but it keeps rising.

00:05:33.132 --> 00:05:33.900
Can you measure it faster?

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:35.702
My anger is also rising.

00:05:35.702 --> 00:05:36.836
Based on my perception of temperature,

00:05:36.836 --> 00:05:38.838
I think it should be 39-40 degrees Celsius. No problem.

00:05:38.838 --> 00:05:40.073
40 degrees is enough, right

00:05:40.073 --> 00:05:41.574
? 40 degrees isn't enough for you?

00:05:41.574 --> 00:05:42.308
I can see

00:05:42.308 --> 00:05:43.409
you're also at 40 degrees.

00:05:43.409 --> 00:05:44.744
I can put it on the building, right

00:05:44.744 --> 00:05:45.678
? No problem.

00:05:45.678 --> 00:05:47.213
The sensor is here, right?

00:05:47.213 --> 00:05:48.881
As long as the sensor doesn't touch the house,

00:05:48.881 --> 00:05:50.350
it should be fine, right

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:51.751
? No problem.

00:05:51.751 --> 00:05:52.885
We spent a little time

00:05:52.885 --> 00:05:54.454
pulling up the data from both sides. Here,

00:05:54.454 --> 00:05:55.321
with shade: 36.7 degrees Celsius. Unshaded: 46.7.

00:05:55.321 --> 00:05:57.090
You can see a significant difference

00:05:57.090 --> 00:05:59.025
in physical heating between

00:05:59.025 --> 00:06:00.827
shaded and unshaded areas.

00:06:00.827 --> 00:06:01.761
Of course, building

00:06:01.761 --> 00:06:03.496
a gazebo on it is fine

00:06:03.496 --> 00:06:04.597
, but

00:06:04.597 --> 00:06:06.032
if you're using solar panels

00:06:06.032 --> 00:06:06.833
,

00:06:06.833 --> 00:06:08.434
there are many methods in the industry.

00:06:08.434 --> 00:06:10.603
One is to rent the site and

00:06:10.603 --> 00:06:12.271
receive a percentage of the revenue

00:06:12.271 --> 00:06:14.440
, or they only pay rent. Another

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:17.009
is for you to build your own

00:06:17.009 --> 00:06:19.145
storage device, which can then

00:06:19.145 --> 00:06:20.146
use your home's electricity.

00:06:20.146 --> 00:06:21.247
Of course, there are many

00:06:21.247 --> 00:06:22.682
different approaches and cooperation methods

00:06:22.682 --> 00:06:24.217
in the industry

00:06:24.217 --> 00:06:25.451
. Again,

00:06:25.451 --> 00:06:26.486
if you're installing

00:06:26.486 --> 00:06:28.154
it on your own roof,

00:06:28.154 --> 00:06:30.089
many online rumors are false

00:06:30.089 --> 00:06:31.791
. The premise is that

00:06:31.791 --> 00:06:33.993
its installation method

00:06:33.993 --> 00:06:35.995
or engineering approach must be correct

00:06:35.995 --> 00:06:36.896
for it to be effective.

00:06:36.896 --> 00:06:38.331
Now let's go indoors.

00:06:39.232 --> 00:06:40.733
Everyone, we're back

00:06:40.733 --> 00:06:42.168
under the roof now.

00:06:42.168 --> 00:06:43.669
We 'll compare two

00:06:43.669 --> 00:06:46.139
completely different environments,

00:06:46.139 --> 00:06:48.441
two identical construction companies, and

00:06:48.441 --> 00:06:49.242
the same environment.

00:06:49.242 --> 00:06:50.977
Now, let's look at the indoor temperature on the rooftop.

00:06:50.977 --> 00:06:52.578
Here,

00:06:52.578 --> 00:06:54.046
there are solar panels

00:06:54.046 --> 00:06:55.448
providing shade.

00:06:55.448 --> 00:06:56.682
What's the temperature now?

00:06:56.682 --> 00:06:58.818
35 degrees Celsius. 35.1 degrees Celsius.

00:06:58.818 --> 00:07:00.052
I think the only difference is ventilation,

00:07:00.052 --> 00:07:02.722
because the windows aren't open,

00:07:02.722 --> 00:07:04.357
so the temperature is slightly higher

00:07:04.357 --> 00:07:05.958
, but still cooler

00:07:05.958 --> 00:07:07.627
than when we were standing in the sun

00:07:07.627 --> 00:07:09.262
. Now let's go to the other side, to

00:07:09.262 --> 00:07:11.297
another rooftop without solar panels.

00:07:11.297 --> 00:07:12.632
What's the temperature

00:07:13.399 --> 00:07:15.234
there? The temperature here is

00:07:15.234 --> 00:07:16.502
38 degrees Celsius. The temperature exceeds

00:07:16.502 --> 00:07:17.904
39 degrees Celsius

00:07:17.904 --> 00:07:20.173
, and next to it is 35 degrees Celsius.

00:07:20.173 --> 00:07:22.975
There seems to be a difference between 39 and 39 degrees

00:07:22.975 --> 00:07:25.645
. After understanding the installation method,

00:07:25.645 --> 00:07:27.480
you will know how the heat inside

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:29.215
your roof will differ

00:07:29.215 --> 00:07:30.316
. However,

00:07:30.316 --> 00:07:31.417
netizens have another issue

00:07:31.417 --> 00:07:33.319
: there is another rumor circulating online

00:07:33.319 --> 00:07:34.787
that solar panels

00:07:34.787 --> 00:07:35.888
are fake

00:07:35.888 --> 00:07:37.390
and completely useless

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:38.357
. The higher the temperature, the

00:07:38.357 --> 00:07:39.792
lower the efficiency.

00:07:39.792 --> 00:07:41.127
Is this true or false?

00:07:41.127 --> 00:07:42.328
Actually, it's not wrong.

00:07:42.328 --> 00:07:43.062
Solar panels

00:07:43.062 --> 00:07:45.164
do indeed decrease in efficiency

00:07:45.164 --> 00:07:46.399
as the temperature rises.

00:07:46.399 --> 00:07:47.333
In Taiwan, the temperature difference

00:07:47.333 --> 00:07:48.634
often exceeds 40 degrees Celsius during

00:07:48.634 --> 00:07:49.702
the summer.

00:07:49.702 --> 00:07:50.770
So, people say that

00:07:50.770 --> 00:07:51.604
in summer, even

00:07:51.604 --> 00:07:53.039
with strong sunlight, it's useless

00:07:53.039 --> 00:07:54.540
because the temperature is so high

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:56.609
that the energy absorbed

00:07:56.609 --> 00:07:57.710
becomes very low,

00:07:57.710 --> 00:08:00.279
and it's basically... That

00:08:00.279 --> 00:08:02.548
's right. The Taiwan Science and Technology Media Center

00:08:02.548 --> 00:08:04.717
once invited experts to explain that

00:08:04.717 --> 00:08:05.985
silicon crystal solar panels

00:08:05.985 --> 00:08:07.086
are actually very sensitive to heat.

00:08:07.086 --> 00:08:08.187
Experiments have shown that

00:08:08.187 --> 00:08:09.489
their optimal condition

00:08:09.489 --> 00:08:10.957
is an air temperature of 25 degrees Celsius. For

00:08:10.957 --> 00:08:12.558
every 1 degree Celsius increase

00:08:12.558 --> 00:08:13.693
in temperature

00:08:13.693 --> 00:08:17.096
, the power generation efficiency decreases by 0.35% - 0.5%.

00:08:17.096 --> 00:08:18.564
In Taiwan, the surface temperature of the panels

00:08:18.564 --> 00:08:20.533
often soars to 45 to 65 degrees Celsius in summer

00:08:20.533 --> 00:08:22.001
, so the efficiency can actually drop by up to

00:08:22.001 --> 00:08:24.704
7%. With a power generation capacity of 10.5%, the

00:08:24.704 --> 00:08:26.572
solar panel we borrowed from a netizen

00:08:26.572 --> 00:08:29.108
uses 19.76kW of solar panels.

00:08:29.108 --> 00:08:29.942
On average, it

00:08:29.942 --> 00:08:31.310
can generate over

00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:32.378
10,000 yuan in electricity

00:08:32.378 --> 00:08:34.080
revenue per month . In the best summer months,

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:36.983
it can generate over 26,000 yuan.

00:08:36.983 --> 00:08:38.184
In less favorable summer months

00:08:38.184 --> 00:08:40.119
, after adding and subtracting,

00:08:40.119 --> 00:08:42.388
the average monthly revenue is still around 10,000 yuan. From

00:08:42.388 --> 00:08:43.055
March to May this year,

00:08:43.055 --> 00:08:45.024
our solar panel generated over 30,000 yuan in

00:08:45.024 --> 00:08:46.792
revenue , so this year's power generation is quite good.

00:08:46.792 --> 00:08:48.728
So, according to what the netizen said

00:08:48.728 --> 00:08:49.862
and the data and reports we saw

00:08:49.862 --> 00:08:51.464
at this technical center,

00:08:51.464 --> 00:08:52.932
which are based on experimental data,

00:08:52.932 --> 00:08:54.433
it's about 50%

00:08:54.433 --> 00:08:55.134
correct.

00:08:55.134 --> 00:08:56.035
Why is it 50

00:08:56.035 --> 00:08:57.103
% correct ? Because

00:08:57.103 --> 00:08:59.372
it is true that the power generation efficiency will decrease due to temperature

00:08:59.372 --> 00:09:01.240
, but the decrease is at most 10%. So why is

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:02.608
the power generation efficiency still better

00:09:02.608 --> 00:09:04.010
in summer

00:09:04.010 --> 00:09:05.611
? You can think of it like this:

00:09:05.611 --> 00:09:06.646
if the full score is 100

00:09:06.646 --> 00:09:07.980
, and you

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:09.515
deduct 10%,

00:09:09.515 --> 00:09:10.850
you

00:09:10.850 --> 00:09:12.118
get 90.

00:09:12.118 --> 00:09:13.185
But summer is long,

00:09:13.185 --> 00:09:15.621
so it's like writing a

00:09:15.621 --> 00:09:17.023
150-point exam. Even with a 9% reduction, the score

00:09:17.023 --> 00:09:18.524
is

00:09:18.524 --> 00:09:19.625
still

00:09:19.625 --> 00:09:22.395
much higher than before.

00:09:22.395 --> 00:09:24.597
Therefore, the electricity collected in summer

00:09:24.597 --> 00:09:26.332
is actually better than in winter,

00:09:26.332 --> 00:09:26.933
a result proven

00:09:26.933 --> 00:09:28.534
by scientific experiments

00:09:28.534 --> 00:09:29.235
. So, do you now

00:09:29.235 --> 00:09:30.570
have a better understanding

00:09:30.570 --> 00:09:31.537
of home solar panels

00:09:31.537 --> 00:09:32.872
? But then

00:09:32.872 --> 00:09:33.739
another claim appears

00:09:33.739 --> 00:09:35.274
online:

00:09:35.274 --> 00:09:36.542
solar panels can't be recycled

00:09:36.542 --> 00:09:38.044
because they're toxic waste

00:09:38.044 --> 00:09:39.545
, or

00:09:39.545 --> 00:09:41.280
what happens to them after they've generated electricity?

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:42.915
Well, next stop, we'll take you to

00:09:42.915 --> 00:09:44.550
a solar panel recycling plant.

00:09:45.084 --> 00:09:45.618
Let's... Now

00:09:45.618 --> 00:09:47.820
we're going to cross two counties

00:09:47.820 --> 00:09:49.822
to take you to a

00:09:49.822 --> 00:09:51.424
solar panel recycling plant.

00:09:51.424 --> 00:09:52.925
The solar panel recycling plant is incredibly ruthless;

00:09:52.925 --> 00:09:54.260
the whole environment might be different

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:55.094
from what you imagine.

00:09:55.094 --> 00:09:56.796
There are actually more than one

00:09:56.796 --> 00:09:57.997
recycling method now

00:09:57.997 --> 00:09:59.165
, but whenever our channel

00:09:59.165 --> 00:10:00.199
talks about solar panels,

00:10:00.199 --> 00:10:02.535
there are always a lot of comments below

00:10:02.535 --> 00:10:04.136
discussing various politics

00:10:04.136 --> 00:10:07.273
and things unrelated to solar panels.

00:10:07.273 --> 00:10:08.975
Actually, many of the problems

00:10:08.975 --> 00:10:10.876
aren't with the solar panels themselves

00:10:10.876 --> 00:10:13.980
, but with the people operating them, the construction companies,

00:10:13.980 --> 00:10:16.082
and some unscrupulous individuals

00:10:16.082 --> 00:10:18.451
trying to profit from the situation.

00:10:18.451 --> 00:10:20.519
Otherwise, why would

00:10:20.519 --> 00:10:22.221
Elon Musk, the world's richest man and owner of Tesla,

00:10:22.221 --> 00:10:23.356
be so enthusiastic about

00:10:23.356 --> 00:10:24.256
solar energy?

00:10:24.256 --> 00:10:25.458
He once said

00:10:25.458 --> 00:10:27.526
that if you cover

00:10:27.526 --> 00:10:29.395
an entire area of ​​the Sahara Desert, a desolate place

00:10:29.395 --> 00:10:30.963
, with solar panels

00:10:30.963 --> 00:10:32.832
, it could provide

00:10:32.832 --> 00:10:35.868
the energy needs of the whole of Europe or even the world.

00:10:35.868 --> 00:10:37.503
If you manage it well,

00:10:37.503 --> 00:10:38.204
it

00:10:38.204 --> 00:10:39.438
can create a good cycle.

00:10:39.438 --> 00:10:40.740
It 's similar to another topic

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:42.408
we'll discuss later

00:10:42.408 --> 00:10:43.843
: plastics. A person

00:10:43.843 --> 00:10:46.112
uses a very small amount of plastic throughout their life

00:10:46.112 --> 00:10:47.313
, repeatedly recycled

00:10:47.313 --> 00:10:48.814
, and it's high-grade plastic—

00:10:48.814 --> 00:10:49.782
BPA-free

00:10:49.782 --> 00:10:51.217
, won't cause penile problems

00:10:51.217 --> 00:10:53.119
, and won't cause

00:10:53.119 --> 00:10:54.654
birth defects

00:10:54.654 --> 00:10:55.988
. If you manage it well

00:10:55.988 --> 00:10:57.023
and create this cycle

00:10:57.023 --> 00:10:58.724
, it can actually help us solve

00:10:58.724 --> 00:11:00.860
many other related problems.

00:11:00.860 --> 00:11:02.828
So the key is how you

00:11:02.828 --> 00:11:03.562
use it. Personally

00:11:03.562 --> 00:11:05.264
, I think solar panels are actually

00:11:05.264 --> 00:11:07.333
... If you use a product

00:11:07.333 --> 00:11:08.434
properly,

00:11:08.434 --> 00:11:10.403
it can make things much easier

00:11:10.403 --> 00:11:11.604
, save you a lot of money

00:11:11.604 --> 00:11:13.172
, or change your life significantly.

00:11:13.172 --> 00:11:15.941
All the lights on my balcony and in

00:11:15.941 --> 00:11:17.510
my backyard are now

00:11:17.510 --> 00:11:18.678
solar-powered.

00:11:18.678 --> 00:11:19.412
Even small ones like these

00:11:19.412 --> 00:11:20.346
are all solar-powered.

00:11:20.346 --> 00:11:21.714
If you add up

00:11:21.714 --> 00:11:23.049
a dozen or twenty

00:11:23.049 --> 00:11:24.183
of these 5-watt

00:11:24.183 --> 00:11:25.117
lights,

00:11:25.117 --> 00:11:26.185
you can save

00:11:26.185 --> 00:11:27.687
several thousand or even tens of thousands of dollars a year.

00:11:27.687 --> 00:11:29.922
Usually, it's the batteries that fail

00:11:29.922 --> 00:11:31.323
first, the rechargeable batteries

00:11:31.323 --> 00:11:33.125
, not the solar panels.

00:11:33.125 --> 00:11:34.627
But solar panels will eventually fail.

00:11:34.627 --> 00:11:35.728
The real replacement cycle

00:11:35.728 --> 00:11:37.830
won't begin now

00:11:37.830 --> 00:11:38.664
,

00:11:38.664 --> 00:11:40.733
but in the next few years, with

00:11:40.733 --> 00:11:42.635
large-scale solar panel replacements

00:11:42.635 --> 00:11:43.402
. Will

00:11:43.402 --> 00:11:44.270
these solar panels

00:11:44.270 --> 00:11:45.805
become the toxic waste everyone talks about

00:11:45.805 --> 00:11:47.673
, or are they completely unrecyclable?

00:11:47.673 --> 00:11:49.208
In 30 minutes,

00:11:49.208 --> 00:11:51.310
we'll arrive at the recycling plant.

00:11:51.310 --> 00:11:52.344
Let's... Seeing

00:11:53.245 --> 00:11:54.980
such a large-scale solar panel recycling operation

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:56.949
is not something you see every day, so

00:11:57.550 --> 00:11:58.317
hurry up and run!

00:12:01.053 --> 00:12:02.655
Of course, there are actually quite a few

00:12:02.655 --> 00:12:03.422
solar panel recycling

00:12:03.422 --> 00:12:04.857
companies, and today we've chosen one

00:12:04.857 --> 00:12:06.092
in central Taiwan.

00:12:06.959 --> 00:12:08.594
How do they recycle solar panels?

00:12:08.594 --> 00:12:10.296
This company we're visiting today boasts a

00:12:10.296 --> 00:12:12.698
recycling rate of over 95%,

00:12:12.698 --> 00:12:15.267
capable of disassembling solar panels into very fine parts

00:12:15.267 --> 00:12:16.902
for complete recycling.

00:12:16.902 --> 00:12:18.070
Today we're showing you a

00:12:18.070 --> 00:12:19.305
small disassembly line

00:12:19.305 --> 00:12:20.773
because the actual disassembly process will

00:12:20.773 --> 00:12:21.540
be a bit noisy

00:12:21.540 --> 00:12:22.975
, so we'll use narration

00:12:22.975 --> 00:12:24.210
to explain

00:12:24.210 --> 00:12:25.511
how solar panels are recycled later

00:12:25.511 --> 00:12:26.312
. Let's... Whenever

00:12:26.312 --> 00:12:27.279
solar panels are mentioned

00:12:27.279 --> 00:12:28.848
online, there are many vivid descriptions

00:12:28.848 --> 00:12:30.049
claiming they are toxic

00:12:30.049 --> 00:12:31.717
or cause disasters.

00:12:31.717 --> 00:12:33.252
Of course, burying them indiscriminately

00:12:33.252 --> 00:12:34.520
will certainly cause harm.

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:35.154
However ,

00:12:35.154 --> 00:12:36.422
there is actually a method for

00:12:36.422 --> 00:12:37.656
recycling solar panels .

00:12:37.656 --> 00:12:39.258
First, you need to understand that a solar panel

00:12:39.258 --> 00:12:40.926
is essentially like a glass window

00:12:40.926 --> 00:12:42.762
; it has a very simple

00:12:42.762 --> 00:12:43.462
sandwich structure

00:12:43.462 --> 00:12:44.163
. The main components

00:12:44.163 --> 00:12:46.632
are glass (74%) ,

00:12:46.632 --> 00:12:47.800
aluminum

00:12:47.800 --> 00:12:48.934
(about 10%

00:12:48.934 --> 00:12:50.503
) (the aluminum frame you see ),

00:12:50.503 --> 00:12:52.071
silicon wafers (very valuable

00:12:52.071 --> 00:12:53.973
, but about 4%)

00:12:53.973 --> 00:12:55.641
(the part responsible for generating electricity)

00:12:55.641 --> 00:12:57.510
, and finally, the non-recyclable parts

00:12:57.510 --> 00:12:58.978
used for bonding and sealing

00:12:58.978 --> 00:13:00.713
—the outer window glass and the inner aluminum frame, which

00:13:00.713 --> 00:13:02.915
is waterproofed by

00:13:02.915 --> 00:13:03.816
EVA plastic film.

00:13:03.816 --> 00:13:04.984
You can think of

00:13:04.984 --> 00:13:06.652
EVA as the EVA inside shoes.

00:13:06.652 --> 00:13:07.219
Basically,

00:13:07.219 --> 00:13:08.521
it makes up a very small

00:13:08.521 --> 00:13:09.555
percentage of the total

00:13:09.555 --> 00:13:11.423
. Therefore, the factory we're filming today

00:13:11.423 --> 00:13:12.858
can

00:13:12.858 --> 00:13:14.360
recycle over 95% of its solar panels

00:13:14.360 --> 00:13:16.562
. The boss just said, "95% is an understatement;

00:13:16.562 --> 00:13:17.863
actually, I can achieve 97%.

00:13:17.863 --> 00:13:18.664
" The remaining 3%

00:13:18.664 --> 00:13:19.565
(including natural losses during processing)

00:13:19.565 --> 00:13:21.967
is what we get. It's actually just EVA

00:13:21.967 --> 00:13:23.135
and other natural losses during the processing.

00:13:23.135 --> 00:13:24.737
The small-scale recycling line we're filming today

00:13:24.737 --> 00:13:25.871
can be broken down into several steps.

00:13:25.871 --> 00:13:27.540
First, disassembling the junction box

00:13:27.540 --> 00:13:28.741
involves using pneumatic tools and

00:13:28.741 --> 00:13:29.875
manual scraping to

00:13:29.875 --> 00:13:31.143
remove it.

00:13:31.143 --> 00:13:31.811
Second,

00:13:31.811 --> 00:13:33.546
using hydraulic pressure

00:13:33.546 --> 00:13:34.747
to pull out the aluminum frame.

00:13:34.747 --> 00:13:35.381
Third,

00:13:35.381 --> 00:13:37.550
removing the glass residue from the aluminum frame

00:13:37.550 --> 00:13:38.617
, and finally scraping off the glass,

00:13:38.617 --> 00:13:40.286
leaving only the silicon wafers and backplane –

00:13:40.286 --> 00:13:41.086
all clean.

00:13:41.420 --> 00:13:42.822
In our factory, you

00:13:42.822 --> 00:13:45.291
can see the final disassembly results in this.

00:13:45.291 --> 00:13:46.392
From these fragments

00:13:46.392 --> 00:13:48.661
, you can extract silicon,

00:13:48.661 --> 00:13:49.829
copper,

00:13:49.829 --> 00:13:50.963
and silver.

00:13:50.963 --> 00:13:51.931
But in this episode,

00:13:51.931 --> 00:13:52.832
I want to tell you

00:13:52.832 --> 00:13:54.600
that the solar energy industry

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:55.501
is actually a

00:13:55.501 --> 00:13:57.136
rolling, emerging industry.

00:13:57.136 --> 00:13:57.970
That is to say,

00:13:57.970 --> 00:13:59.171
20- The technology of 30 years ago

00:13:59.171 --> 00:14:00.739
is certainly different from that of today.

00:14:00.739 --> 00:14:02.908
The recycling methods of 30 years ago and today

00:14:02.908 --> 00:14:04.243
have also been constantly evolving

00:14:04.243 --> 00:14:04.910
and improving

00:14:04.910 --> 00:14:06.679
. The technology of solar panels themselves

00:14:06.679 --> 00:14:07.580
may not have had very

00:14:07.580 --> 00:14:08.347
good absorption

00:14:08.347 --> 00:14:09.148
and conversion rates

00:14:09.148 --> 00:14:11.050
in the past , but year after year... in fact,

00:14:11.050 --> 00:14:12.117
it has become increasingly better.

00:14:12.117 --> 00:14:13.252
The recycling technology

00:14:13.252 --> 00:14:14.753
you see now is just one example

00:14:14.753 --> 00:14:16.155
, but in the same factory,

00:14:16.155 --> 00:14:17.089
their recycling technology

00:14:17.089 --> 00:14:18.190
can

00:14:18.190 --> 00:14:19.825
now

00:14:19.825 --> 00:14:20.926
achieve this.

00:14:20.926 --> 00:14:22.895
Can you see how clean it is? Then

00:14:25.130 --> 00:14:26.632
you can extract the silver

00:14:26.632 --> 00:14:28.467
and copper from it

00:14:28.467 --> 00:14:29.435
within the factory grounds,

00:14:29.435 --> 00:14:31.670
which is equivalent to one kilogram of solar energy. A solar panel

00:14:31.670 --> 00:14:32.571
is a whole piece like this,

00:14:32.571 --> 00:14:33.305
weighing one kilogram

00:14:33.305 --> 00:14:35.374
. You can take 1 to 4 grams

00:14:35.374 --> 00:14:37.376
and pull it out in strips, like this.

00:14:37.376 --> 00:14:38.077
When you recycle silver,

00:14:38.077 --> 00:14:38.811
you

00:14:38.811 --> 00:14:40.246
can further refine it

00:14:40.246 --> 00:14:41.213
into pure silver.

00:14:41.213 --> 00:14:42.047
Silver is very expensive now

00:14:42.047 --> 00:14:43.215
; how much is one gram of silver?

00:14:43.215 --> 00:14:45.384
During the gold rush a while ago,

00:14:45.384 --> 00:14:46.318
gold was over 5000,

00:14:46.318 --> 00:14:47.353
and silver was incredibly expensive.

00:14:48.454 --> 00:14:49.722
Of course, you can also refine copper.

00:14:49.722 --> 00:14:51.056
Then there are the commonly seen

00:14:51.056 --> 00:14:52.358
recycled materials like glass and aluminum.

00:14:52.358 --> 00:14:53.158
You should have a good grasp

00:14:53.158 --> 00:14:54.627
of the recycling process

00:14:54.627 --> 00:14:55.461
. Returning to what I just mentioned,

00:14:55.461 --> 00:14:57.696
this industry is constantly changing.

00:14:57.696 --> 00:14:58.797
That is to say, whether it's

00:14:58.797 --> 00:15:00.199
the installation method

00:15:00.199 --> 00:15:02.268
, the manufacturing of the solar panels

00:15:02.268 --> 00:15:03.269
, or recycling

00:15:03.269 --> 00:15:04.403
, it's actually a yearly process...

00:15:04.403 --> 00:15:05.271
Previously,

00:15:05.271 --> 00:15:06.205
we encountered this problem:

00:15:06.205 --> 00:15:07.573
the solar panels couldn't withstand wind damage.

00:15:07.573 --> 00:15:08.941
So, what should we do

00:15:08.941 --> 00:15:10.743
now? Previously, these materials couldn't be recycled this way

00:15:10.743 --> 00:15:11.877
. So, how should we proceed

00:15:11.877 --> 00:15:14.313
? It's actually part of a technology supply chain

00:15:14.313 --> 00:15:15.814
, and everyone is constantly

00:15:15.814 --> 00:15:17.449
updating...

00:15:17.449 --> 00:15:18.584
Now, on the back of the solar panel,

00:15:18.584 --> 00:15:19.685
you'll see a barcode

00:15:19.685 --> 00:15:20.319
.

00:15:20.319 --> 00:15:21.520
You can think of this barcode as a

00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:22.221
birth certificate

00:15:22.221 --> 00:15:23.289
. That is,

00:15:23.289 --> 00:15:25.658
when the solar panel is manufactured,

00:15:25.658 --> 00:15:28.661
the manufacturer also bears the recycling cost.

00:15:28.661 --> 00:15:29.428
You can think of it as

00:15:29.428 --> 00:15:30.529
a funeral allowance.

00:15:30.529 --> 00:15:32.364
When your child is born,

00:15:32.364 --> 00:15:33.899
you have to pay a sum of money to the government

00:15:33.899 --> 00:15:34.833
so that

00:15:34.833 --> 00:15:37.036
everyone can have a coffin, be

00:15:37.036 --> 00:15:38.404
cremated,

00:15:38.404 --> 00:15:40.339
and be buried

00:15:40.339 --> 00:15:41.707
in a columbarium.

00:15:41.707 --> 00:15:42.374
This is a prepayment.

00:15:42.374 --> 00:15:43.242
In

00:15:43.242 --> 00:15:44.310
the past,

00:15:44.310 --> 00:15:45.711
there were cases of people littering

00:15:45.711 --> 00:15:46.712
. Now, since

00:15:46.712 --> 00:15:49.014
the recycling cost is included,

00:15:49.014 --> 00:15:50.482
you can just throw it to a recycling company for collection,

00:15:50.482 --> 00:15:51.951
because the money is already included.

00:15:51.951 --> 00:15:54.620
But now that there's a funeral allowance, if

00:15:54.620 --> 00:15:56.155
you still leave unidentified bodies

00:15:56.155 --> 00:15:57.723
or litter them, you'll

00:15:57.723 --> 00:15:58.524
be fined

00:15:58.524 --> 00:15:59.391
3 million

00:15:59.391 --> 00:16:00.626
, meaning you'll be fined for one year

00:16:00.626 --> 00:16:02.261
... So, you see, there are these unscrupulous people.

00:16:02.261 --> 00:16:03.429
How do we stop them from

00:16:03.429 --> 00:16:04.863
causing such engineering problems

00:16:04.863 --> 00:16:06.298
? How do we solve them

00:16:06.298 --> 00:16:08.334
? Of course, you can imagine that with current technology,

00:16:08.334 --> 00:16:09.435
a solar panel

00:16:09.435 --> 00:16:11.036
can achieve 95%

00:16:11.036 --> 00:16:12.504
to 97% purity, as the boss mentioned.

00:16:12.504 --> 00:16:14.673
Only 3% of EVA cannot be recycled.

00:16:14.673 --> 00:16:16.408
So, what people may not understand

00:16:16.408 --> 00:16:18.444
is silicon

00:16:18.444 --> 00:16:19.511
. You might think of

00:16:19.511 --> 00:16:20.312
TSMC

00:16:20.312 --> 00:16:21.113
semiconductors

00:16:21.113 --> 00:16:22.748
, or you might think of glass,

00:16:22.748 --> 00:16:23.649
or you might think of

00:16:23.649 --> 00:16:24.450
silicone. The

00:16:24.450 --> 00:16:25.584
silicone that electricians make

00:16:25.584 --> 00:16:26.151
is also silicon.

00:16:26.151 --> 00:16:27.219
Of course, the degree

00:16:27.219 --> 00:16:28.754
and purity are different, and

00:16:28.754 --> 00:16:29.755
the methods of application are different.

00:16:29.755 --> 00:16:31.156
But actually, silicon itself

00:16:31.156 --> 00:16:31.957
is non-toxic.

00:16:31.957 --> 00:16:33.692
So, under normal use,

00:16:33.692 --> 00:16:35.527
normal production and manufacturing,

00:16:35.527 --> 00:16:37.963
if it doesn't come from random places,

00:16:37.963 --> 00:16:40.199
and you recycle it properly,

00:16:40.199 --> 00:16:42.167
install it according to normal

00:16:42.167 --> 00:16:44.770
specifications, let it serve for decades,

00:16:44.770 --> 00:16:45.704
and after it's over,

00:16:45.704 --> 00:16:48.240
dismantle it properly to become the next product

00:16:48.240 --> 00:16:48.974
in a normal cycle,

00:16:48.974 --> 00:16:50.209
there won't be any problems.

00:16:50.209 --> 00:16:51.176
So, the problem is with the

00:16:51.176 --> 00:16:52.077
people.

00:16:52.077 --> 00:16:53.345
When we talk about the problem with people,

00:16:53.345 --> 00:16:54.413
in the previous episodes on

00:16:54.413 --> 00:16:55.781
solar panel information,

00:16:55.781 --> 00:16:56.382
everyone mentioned that

00:16:56.382 --> 00:16:58.183
you know about central and southern Taiwan.

00:16:58.183 --> 00:17:00.152
The story of

00:17:00.152 --> 00:17:01.587
"fake aquaculture, real subsidies"

00:17:01.587 --> 00:17:03.389
and "fake aquaculture, real electricity sales"

00:17:03.389 --> 00:17:05.324
—discarding your fishponds

00:17:05.324 --> 00:17:06.658
and turning them into solar power plants—

00:17:06.658 --> 00:17:07.626
is something we hear

00:17:07.626 --> 00:17:09.428
every time we discuss this topic.

00:17:09.428 --> 00:17:10.662
Returning to what I just said,

00:17:10.662 --> 00:17:11.563
this industry undergoes a lot of

00:17:11.563 --> 00:17:12.598
continuous adjustments.

00:17:12.598 --> 00:17:13.499
Initially,

00:17:13.499 --> 00:17:14.767
everyone envisioned aquaculture-solar co-production

00:17:14.767 --> 00:17:16.035
as something wonderful

00:17:16.035 --> 00:17:16.668
, but

00:17:16.668 --> 00:17:19.138
many solar power operators had no experience in fish farming,

00:17:19.138 --> 00:17:20.305
so they didn't know how to do it.

00:17:20.305 --> 00:17:22.508
Plus, there were many unscrupulous individuals

00:17:22.508 --> 00:17:23.876
—some wanting to exploit it

00:17:23.876 --> 00:17:25.177
for personal gain

00:17:25.177 --> 00:17:26.912
, others simply

00:17:26.912 --> 00:17:28.080
completing the project and running away.

00:17:28.080 --> 00:17:29.081
But if we're

00:17:29.081 --> 00:17:30.949
talking about

00:17:30.949 --> 00:17:33.118
how to do aquaculture-solar co-production well,

00:17:33.118 --> 00:17:34.353
let's continue on the highway

00:17:34.353 --> 00:17:35.654
to southern Taiwan.

00:17:36.221 --> 00:17:37.556
Next, we'll show you a

00:17:37.556 --> 00:17:38.590
case study of aquaculture-solar co-production

00:17:38.590 --> 00:17:39.658
that immediately comes to mind

00:17:39.658 --> 00:17:41.026
when talking about central and southern

00:17:41.026 --> 00:17:41.760
Taiwan. We've invited

00:17:41.760 --> 00:17:43.996
Mr. Yeh Chi-tien, Executive Director of

00:17:43.996 --> 00:17:45.731
the Kaohsiung City Da-A-Lian Aquaculture Fisheries Development Association

00:17:45.731 --> 00:17:47.032
. This aquaculture-solar co-production

00:17:47.032 --> 00:17:48.133
site is

00:17:48.133 --> 00:17:50.569
about 1.1 hectares (about 1.1 hectares).

00:17:50.569 --> 00:17:51.637
It's divided into two ponds.

00:17:51.637 --> 00:17:53.672
The design was based on

00:17:53.672 --> 00:17:54.840
the government's principle of "

00:17:54.840 --> 00:17:57.576
aquaculture as the foundation, green energy added value

00:17:57.576 --> 00:17:59.711
," and the design followed this principle

00:17:59.711 --> 00:18:02.247
. Friends online often say that the fish

00:18:02.247 --> 00:18:04.183
in the aquaculture-electro-hydro-water systems in central and southern Taiwan

00:18:04.183 --> 00:18:05.884
are absolutely swarming

00:18:05.884 --> 00:18:07.820
, so I can only describe

00:18:07.820 --> 00:18:10.189
your two ponds' harvest this

00:18:10.189 --> 00:18:10.823
year in three words:

00:18:10.823 --> 00:18:12.558
you 've made

00:18:12.558 --> 00:18:14.059
a killing!

00:18:14.059 --> 00:18:15.961
Do you mean

00:18:15.961 --> 00:18:17.296
the electricity made a killing, or

00:18:17.296 --> 00:18:18.163
the fish?

00:18:18.163 --> 00:18:21.600
The electricity is because we lease the aquaculture-electro-water-water systems to the company

00:18:21.600 --> 00:18:23.001
, so we only earn rent.

00:18:23.001 --> 00:18:24.103
As for the fish, whether

00:18:24.103 --> 00:18:26.338
or not solar panels are installed,

00:18:26.338 --> 00:18:27.573
the fish-raising method is the same;

00:18:27.573 --> 00:18:28.373
there's no need to change it.

00:18:28.373 --> 00:18:29.908
Speaking of the design,

00:18:29.908 --> 00:18:31.477
when building it, we need to consider

00:18:31.477 --> 00:18:33.078
three principles for aquaculture:

00:18:33.078 --> 00:18:33.812
first,

00:18:33.812 --> 00:18:35.981
the aquaculture-electro-water-water system must be operational and able to support aquaculture;

00:18:35.981 --> 00:18:37.916
second, it must be able to harvest,

00:18:37.916 --> 00:18:40.319
because fish and shrimp need to be caught;

00:18:40.319 --> 00:18:42.054
and third, you must have a way to manage

00:18:42.054 --> 00:18:43.322
the sludge underneath—

00:18:43.322 --> 00:18:44.857
you can't let it accumulate,

00:18:44.857 --> 00:18:46.024
you have to dig it up.

00:18:46.024 --> 00:18:47.226
So when we designed

00:18:47.226 --> 00:18:48.794
it, you see, between the pillars

00:18:48.794 --> 00:18:49.928
we designed a 6-meter

00:18:49.928 --> 00:18:52.464
soil turner, which can turn the soil

00:18:52.464 --> 00:18:53.832
and allow for sun exposure.

00:18:53.832 --> 00:18:56.301
The pillar height is 4 meters.

00:18:56.301 --> 00:18:57.903
If our soil is too wet,

00:18:57.903 --> 00:18:58.871
the soil turner can't

00:18:58.871 --> 00:18:59.738
get in, but the excavator can,

00:18:59.738 --> 00:19:01.673
and it won't get stuck on the solar panels.

00:19:01.673 --> 00:19:04.343
Based on our two years of experience,

00:19:04.343 --> 00:19:06.545
we feel that this makes fish and shrimp easier to raise,

00:19:06.545 --> 00:19:07.779
because in southern Taiwan,

00:19:07.779 --> 00:19:10.816
summer temperatures sometimes soar to 36 degrees Celsius. - The temperature is 38 degrees Celsius

00:19:10.816 --> 00:19:13.051
because the solar panels cast a shadow.

00:19:13.051 --> 00:19:14.019
We're storing water,

00:19:14.019 --> 00:19:15.854
usually to a depth of about 3 meters,

00:19:15.854 --> 00:19:17.723
so the fish and shrimp come to the shade. The water temperature here

00:19:17.723 --> 00:19:20.626
isn't as high

00:19:20.626 --> 00:19:21.660
as it would be in the open air.

00:19:21.660 --> 00:19:23.095
So this year's harvest is

00:19:23.095 --> 00:19:23.862
, I feel,

00:19:23.862 --> 00:19:24.997
very, very good,

00:19:24.997 --> 00:19:26.298
especially the Thai shrimp.

00:19:26.298 --> 00:19:28.000
I heard from our colleagues in Pingtung

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:30.302
that their Thai shrimp are so hot they're practically cooked for braised dishes. We

00:19:30.302 --> 00:19:32.571
don't see that here.

00:19:32.571 --> 00:19:33.772
Actually, even without Thai shrimp,

00:19:33.772 --> 00:19:34.773
I can feel it myself

00:19:34.773 --> 00:19:36.508
. Standing here now, I feel

00:19:36.508 --> 00:19:38.510
a significant difference

00:19:38.510 --> 00:19:39.178
compared to when I was outside.

00:19:39.178 --> 00:19:40.145
I feel at least

00:19:40.145 --> 00:19:41.947
5 degrees Celsius.

00:19:41.947 --> 00:19:42.981
5 degrees is a

00:19:42.981 --> 00:19:43.949
huge difference.

00:19:43.949 --> 00:19:45.017
If it were like August,

00:19:45.017 --> 00:19:45.617
you'd be

00:19:45.617 --> 00:19:46.552
sweating buckets

00:19:46.552 --> 00:19:47.819
standing there, you'd fall asleep.

00:19:47.819 --> 00:19:50.389
Today it's probably around 37 degrees Celsius.

00:19:50.389 --> 00:19:51.190
The reason it's not good today is because

00:19:51.190 --> 00:19:52.491
we've already harvested

00:19:52.491 --> 00:19:53.525
, made money, and

00:19:53.525 --> 00:19:54.493
the water level has dropped.

00:19:55.427 --> 00:19:56.495
Are there still shrimp in there? Yes,

00:19:56.495 --> 00:19:57.629
there are still shrimp.

00:19:57.629 --> 00:19:59.131
Wait a minute, let's use one

00:19:59.131 --> 00:20:00.732
